@@ -0,0 +1,17 @@
+# DScape content model
+
+Every post uses the same front matter, so the homepage grid, filters and maps can be built from it.
+Templates: `docs/templates/snapshot.md` and `docs/templates/story.md`.
+
+| Field | Required | Meaning |
+| --- | --- | --- |
+| `kind` | yes | `snapshot` (one image + short caption) or `story` (short blog post) |
+| `categories` | yes | Primary mission or data source, one value (Sentinel-2, CAMS, ...) |
+| `tags` | yes | Topics, places, secondary missions |
+| `image` | yes* | Thumbnail for the grid and social preview (`path`, `alt`). *Missing = site default |
+| `acquired` | EO posts | Acquisition date `"YYYY-MM-DD"` or range `"YYYY-MM-DD/YYYY-MM-DD"` (quoted) |
+| `location` | EO posts | `{ name, lat, lon }`, approximate scene centre |
+| `credit` | EO posts | Data attribution, e.g. "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2026)" |
+| `linkedin` | no | URL of the LinkedIn cross-post |
+
+Images live in `assets/img/<post-slug>/`, never hot-linked from LinkedIn or other sites.
diff --git a/docs/templates/snapshot.md b/docs/templates/snapshot.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..4caff2f
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/templates/snapshot.md
@@ -0,0 +1,21 @@
+---
+# Copy to _posts/YYYY-MM-DD-short-slug.md and fill in. The docs/ folder is not published.
+title: Short, specific title
+date: 2026-01-31 12:00:00 +0100
+kind: snapshot                 # snapshot = one image + short caption
+categories: [Sentinel-2]       # primary mission: Sentinel-1/2/3/5P, CAMS, Landsat, ...
+tags: [fire, portugal]         # topics, places; secondary missions go here too
+image:                         # grid thumbnail + social preview; 1200x630 crop works best
+  path: /assets/img/slug/slug_banner.webp
+  alt: What the image shows, in one sentence
+acquired: "2026-01-30"         # one date, or a range "2026-01-28/2026-01-30"
+location: { name: "Place, Country", lat: 0.0, lon: 0.0 }
+credit: "Contains modified Copernicus Sentinel data (2026)"
+linkedin:                      # optional: URL of the LinkedIn cross-post
+comments: true
+---
+
+![What the image shows](/assets/img/slug/slug.webp)
+_One-line caption. Credits: Copernicus Sentinel-2_
+
+One to three sentences: what happened, where, when, and what to look at in the image.
